WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.420
Someone attacks you.

2
00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.630
You defend yourself,
and your attacker dies.

3
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:07.300
A bomber pilot destroys a weapons factory,

4
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:10.500
foreseeing that some
nearby civilians will die.

5
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.730
Both acts cost a life.

6
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.310
Are they wrong, or can they be right?

7
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.310
Can an act that causes
a death still be good,

8
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.880
if the death was not what you aimed at?

9
00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:25.000
In this mission, you'll read what
Thomas Aquinas wrote about self-defence,

10
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.840
and why it still matters.

11
00:00:26.890 --> 00:00:30.230
Then you'll put 4 conditions
to the test on hard cases,

12
00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.210
from war to medicine.

13
00:00:32.260 --> 00:00:37.510
Your mission: find out when, if ever,
an act that causes a death can still be

14
00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:38.110
good.
